Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 16:48:16 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: power: supply: apple,tristar-charger: Add USB
 role switch

On the iPad 5 the Lightning port is either the USB device (DWC2) or, for
the Lightning-to-USB camera adapter, a USB host (EHCI/OHCI), and a role
switch moves it between the two. The adapter announces itself over the
Lightning ID bus, which the charger's Tristar (CBTL1610) masters, so the
charger is where the decision is made.

The charger already sets the device controller's role through its port.
Add an optional phandle to the role switch that gives the PHY to the
host controllers; while the port is a host, the device controller stays
off. A board without it (the iPad 6) keeps the port a USB device and
identifies no accessory.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 .../bindings/power/supply/apple,tristar-charger.yaml  | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/power/supply/apple,tristar-charger.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/power/supply/apple,tristar-charger.yaml
index c839ad0ac..59bc52c42 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/power/supply/apple,tristar-charger.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/power/supply/apple,tristar-charger.yaml
@@ -60,6 +60,17 @@ properties:
     $ref: /schemas/types.yaml#/definitions/phandle
     description: The Tristar (CBTL1610) port controller on its I2C bus.
 
+  apple,usb-role-switch:
+    $ref: /schemas/types.yaml#/definitions/phandle
+    description: |
+      The role switch that gives the Lightning port's PHY to the USB host
+      controllers, such as the Apple S8000 USB role switch. When present, the
+      charger also identifies Lightning accessories over the Tristar ID bus
+      and makes the port a USB host while a camera adapter is attached, as
+      iOS does; the adapter then is the power source, and the device
+      controller linked through port stays off. Without it, the port stays a
+      USB device and no accessory is identified.
+
   input-current-limit-microamp:
     description: Board maximum input current.
 
